---
// Homepage hero (PROJECT_BRIEF.md Section 5 "Homepage — LOCKED", item 1).
// Content is final per the brief (Section 6): role line, intro, CTA, and
// tags. Rebuilt to a precise 12-column grid spec (a target wireframe the
// file attached), replacing the earlier freeform version.
//
// "Motion Design" was dropped from the tag list per direct request - two
// tags now, not three. Nothing else in this file assumes a specific tag
// count (the list wraps via plain flexbox), so removing one needed no
// layout changes.
//
// Grid: shares --intro-max-width / --intro-margin with Header.astro (see
// global.css) so logo, nav/CV, the title, and the bottom block all sit on
// the same margin lines — the earlier version's biggest complaint was
// that these drifted out of alignment with each other.
//
// The visual anchor is now a portrait image slot (replacing the earlier
// organic placeholder blob — a mistake in the sketch this rebuilt from,
// per direct correction) with "PORTFOLIO" overlapping its lower third,
// the same locked object-in-letterform device as before, just a
// different placeholder shape. The word is sized with container query
// units (cqw) rather than a hand-tuned clamp() curve, so it fills the
// full grid width edge-to-edge without overflowing or wrapping at any
// viewport width — a plain-clamp() fallback covers browsers without
// container query support.
//
// Motion: this is the project's first real use of GSAP (previously
// plumbing-only, see src/utils/motion.ts). Every animated property is
// transform/opacity/clip-path only (GPU-only, no layout impact). All
// initial "hidden" states are set imperatively via gsap.set() in the
// script below, never in static CSS — so if JS fails to load, everything
// still renders in its normal, final, fully visible position. See the
// prefersReducedMotion() guard for the reduced-motion path.
//
// Open decisions this component had to fill in (not locked anywhere —
// see CLAUDE.md "Open decisions"):
// - No real photo exists yet (PROJECT_BRIEF.md Section 6) — the image
//   slot is a placeholder block with a TODO showing the exact swap-in
//   markup once one exists.
//
// The "Get to know me" CTA that used to live here is gone - direct
// request ("remove the cta from the hero at the top and place it
// underneath the design principles"), relocated to Principles.astro (see
// that file's own comment) rather than duplicated. The "(Scroll)" cue
// stays - it's a scroll hint, not a call-to-action, and wasn't part of
// the request. It no longer needs its own row wrapper to share a line
// with a button that's gone; it's just a right-aligned line on its own
// now.
import Gallery from './Gallery.astro';

const titleWord = 'Portfolio';
const letters = titleWord.split('');
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__visual">
      <h1 class="hero__title" aria-label={titleWord}>
        <span class="hero__title-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          {letters.map((letter) => (
            <span class="hero__letter-mask">
              <span class="hero__letter">{letter}</span>
            </span>
          ))}
        </span>
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__bottom">
      <p class="hero__role">Experience designer</p>

      <!--
        Echoes Header's own location/availability line
        (Header.astro's .site-header__status). Per direct request the
        reading order here is now role -> location -> paragraph -> tools
        on every screen size, not just mobile (this used to be
        mobile-only, hidden on desktop/tablet in favor of the header's
        own copy) - it now always shows, right under the role line.
      -->
      <p class="hero__status">
        <svg class="hero__status-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path
            d="M8 14.2C8 14.2 12.5 9.8 12.5 6.3C12.5 3.8 10.5 1.8 8 1.8C5.5 1.8 3.5 3.8 3.5 6.3C3.5 9.8 8 14.2 8 14.2Z"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.2"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          />
          <circle cx="8" cy="6.3" r="1.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" />
        </svg>
        Belgium <span aria-hidden="true">|</span> Available Feb 2027
      </p>

      <p class="hero__intro">
        I find ideas in the knot, and the solution usually somewhere that isn't design. Currently in
        my 3rd year at Devine.
      </p>

      <!--
        Moved here from About's own dedicated Tools section, per direct
        request ("I think I should include them at the top of the page
        close to the experience designer to-be paragraph") - a plain row
        of icons rather than the bracket-tag chips the About version
        used ("the tools can be just icons like in this example"), still
        placeholder (no real toolkit confirmed yet - see the removed
        AboutTools.astro's own history in AGENTS.md for why). Per a later
        direct request it no longer sits beside the role line on desktop
        (grid_column 8/13, sharing row 1) - it now sits in the same
        column as the role/status/intro above it, after the paragraph,
        so the reading order (role, location, paragraph, tools) is
        identical at every viewport width instead of desktop having its
        own separate order.
      -->
      <div class="hero__tools">
        <p class="hero__tools-label">Tools</p>
        <ul class="hero__tools-list">
          {Array.from({ length: 5 }).map((_, i) => (
            <li>
              <span class="hero__tools-icon" aria-label={`Tool ${i + 1}`}>
                <!-- TODO: replace with a real tool icon once the toolkit is supplied -->
              </span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!--
        Used to also hold the "Get to know me" button, sharing this row
        via justify-content: space-between (button left, scroll cue
        pushed right). That button is gone now (relocated to
        Principles.astro - see this file's header comment), so the row
        keeps only the scroll cue, right-aligned via justify-content:
        flex-end instead.
      -->
      <div class="hero__cta-row">
        <span class="hero__scroll">(Scroll)</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!--
      The Gallery strip lives here now, replacing the old portrait and
      floating chip - per feedback that the two random floating images
      said nothing, and the gallery is proof of work.
    -->
    <div class="hero__gallery">
      <Gallery embedded />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import { gsap, prefersReducedMotion } from '../../utils/motion';

  const hero = document.querySelector('.hero');
  if (hero) {
    const letters = hero.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.hero__letter');
    const gallery = hero.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.hero__gallery');
    const bottom = hero.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.hero__bottom');

    if (!prefersReducedMotion() && letters.length && gallery && bottom) {
      // Initial states live here, not in CSS, so if this script never runs
      // the hero renders fully visible in its final layout.
      gsap.set(letters, { yPercent: 115 });
      gsap.set([gallery, bottom], { autoAlpha: 0, y: 24 });

      gsap
        .timeline()
        .to(
          letters,
          {
            yPercent: 0,
            duration: 0.9,
            ease: 'back.out(1.5)',
            stagger: { each: 0.045, from: 'start', ease: 'sine.inOut' },
          },
          0.15,
        )
        .to(gallery, { autoAlpha: 1, y: 0, duration: 0.9, ease: 'power2.out' }, 0.55)
        .to(bottom, { autoAlpha: 1, y: 0, duration: 0.8, ease: 'power2.out' }, 0.8);
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }

  .hero__inner {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--intro-max-width);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--intro-margin);
    padding-block: var(--space-32);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    gap: var(--space-32);
  }

  .hero__visual {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    column-gap: var(--intro-gutter);
    row-gap: var(--space-16);
  }

  /* Full-width, edge-to-edge title. container-type turns on cqw sizing for .hero__title-visual below — the word's font-size tracks this element's own rendered width, not the viewport, so it fills the grid at any width from 320px to well past 2560px without a hand-tuned breakpoint ladder. The negative margin-top is in em (title's own font-size), not px or %, so the overlap into the image's lower third scales with the word instead of drifting at other viewports. */
  .hero__title {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    grid-row: 1;
    container-type: inline-size;
    /* Without this, the negative margin-top below collapses straight through the h1 (standard block margin-collapsing), leaving the h1 measuring 0 height and the word floating detached from the grid's own row-sizing. flow-root opts out of collapsing without clipping the intentional overflow into the row above. */
    display: flow-root;
    /* Deliberately no position/z-index here: either one establishes a new stacking context, which would isolate .hero__letter's mix-blend-mode from the image and page background behind it (it would only blend against other things inside .hero__title, which is nothing) — paint order alone (title comes after image in the markup) already puts it on top. */
  }

  .hero__title-visual {
    display: flex;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 0.8;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* 27cqw is measured, not guessed: at a given font-size, "PORTFOLIO" in this display font/weight/tracking renders to ~3.71x that font-size in width, so 100 / 3.71 ~= 27 is the cqw value that makes the rendered word width match the container width (edge to edge). The clamp() bounds are a floor/ceiling safety net, not the fallback — that's @supports below. */
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 27cqw, 26rem);
  }

  .hero__letter-mask {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero__letter {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* Fallback for browsers without container query units: a viewport-based clamp() curve, same floor/ceiling as the cqw version above. */
  @supports not (container-type: inline-size) {
    .hero__title-visual {
      font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 11vw + 1rem, 26rem);
    }
  }

  .hero__gallery {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .hero__bottom {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    column-gap: var(--intro-gutter);
  }

  .hero__role {
    grid-column: 1 / 6;
    grid-row: 1;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.5vw, 1.25rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* role -> location -> paragraph -> tools, in that order on every
     screen width (explicit grid-row per element rather than relying on
     DOM order + auto-placement, so the sequence can't silently drift if
     a future edit reorders the markup). Used to sit beside .hero__role
     in its own column (8/13, sharing row 1) and only show on mobile at
     all - per direct request it's now always visible, directly under
     the role line, matching Header's own .site-header__status copy. */
  .hero__status {
    grid-column: 1 / 6;
    grid-row: 2;
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    width: fit-content;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4em;
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-left: 0.85rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .hero__status::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.2em;
    bottom: 0.2em;
    width: var(--border-hairline);
    background: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .hero__status-icon {
    width: 0.9em;
    height: 0.9em;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hero__status span {
    margin-inline: 0.15em;
  }

  .hero__intro {
    grid-column: 1 / 6;
    grid-row: 3;
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    max-width: 38ch;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.95rem + 0.3vw, 1.125rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  /* Now stacked below the paragraph (same 1/6 column, row 4), not beside
     the role line - per direct request that it "not be on the right
     like that" on desktop. */
  .hero__tools {
    grid-column: 1 / 6;
    grid-row: 4;
    margin-top: var(--space-24);
  }

  .hero__tools-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .hero__tools-list {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .hero__tools-icon {
    display: block;
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 2.25rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-text-secondary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-image);
  }

  /* Full-width row, per-breakpoint override no longer needed (unlike
     when it also held the CTA button) - just the scroll cue, pushed to
     the right via justify-content: flex-end. */
  .hero__cta-row {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    grid-row: 5;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    margin-top: var(--space-48);
  }

  .hero__scroll {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) and (max-width: 1023px) {
    .hero__inner {
      /* Same fix as the mobile block below, for the same reason: the base rule's 100dvh space-between is a desktop-only ask (see the mobile comment), but this range never got the override — on a portrait tablet (820x1100 measured) it left a ~265px dead gap between the image/title and the role/intro/CTA block. */
      justify-content: flex-start;
    }

    .hero__bottom {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
    }

    /* Same role -> status -> intro -> tools -> CTA row order as the base
                                                                 rule (unchanged here, just a wider column span) - only the column
                                                                 range needs overriding for the narrower 7-column grid.
                                                                 .hero__cta-row already spans 1 / -1 at every width, so it needs
                                                                 no override here. */
    .hero__role,
    .hero__status,
    .hero__intro,
    .hero__tools {
      grid-column: 1 / 8;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .hero__inner {
      justify-content: flex-start;
    }

    .hero__visual {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .hero__bottom {
      /* Grid becomes irrelevant here - a plain block stack follows the
                                                                                                                             markup's own DOM order (role, status, intro, tools, CTA, scroll),
                                                                                                                             which is already the same role -> location -> paragraph -> tools
                                                                                                                             order the base rule's explicit grid-rows give every wider
                                                                                                                             breakpoint, so nothing here needs to re-specify row/column
                                                                                                                             placement the way it used to. */
      display: block;
      margin-top: var(--space-32);
    }

    .hero__intro {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
</style>
